
~(binf-flag)
~(gnome-door)

%% Anchoring the balloon

(unlikely [tie #wire-coil to $hook])
	(hook $hook)
(unlikely [untie #wire-coil])

(prevent [tie #braided-wire to $hook])
	(hook $hook)
	(#braided-wire is #tiedto $hook)
	The balloon is already tied up.

(perform [tie #braided-wire to $hook])
	(hook $hook)
	(now) (#braided-wire is #tiedto $hook)
	The balloon is fastened to the hook.

(perform [untie #braided-wire])
	(#braided-wire is #tiedto $)
	(now) (#braided-wire is #partof #basket2)
	The wire falls off the hook.

(prevent [leave $Here $Dir by $Vehicle])
	($Vehicle = #basket2)
	(from $Here go $Dir to $Room)
	~($Room is midair)
	I'm afraid you can't control the balloon in this way.

(prevent [leave $ $ by $Vehicle])
	($Vehicle = #basket2)
	(balloon is anchored)
	The balloon is tied to the hook.

%% Moving the balloon

(perform [burn $obj with $])
	($obj is #in #receptacle)
	(The $obj) burns inside the receptacle.
	The cloth bag inflates as it fills with hot air.
	(now) (binf-flag)

(balloon is anchored)
	(#braided-wire is #tiedto $)

(balloon stops $stops)
	($stops = [#volcano-bottom #volcano-core1 #volcano-core2 #volcano-core3 #volcano-core4])

(balloon rises)
	(#basket2 is #in #volcano-core4)
	(par)
	Your balloon has hit the rim of the volcano, ripping the cloth and
	causing you a 500 foot drop. Did you get your flight insurance?
	(jigs up)

(balloon rises)
	(#basket2 is #in $room)
	(balloon stops $stops)
	(split $stops by $room into $ and [$newroom | $])
	(par)
	The balloon ascends.
	(enter $newroom by #basket2)

(balloon falls)
	(#basket2 is #in $room)
	(balloon stops $stops)
	(split $stops by $room into $prev and $)
	(last $prev $newroom)
	(par)
	The balloon descends.
	(enter $newroom by #basket2)

(on every tick)
	(#player is #in #basket2)
	~(balloon is anchored)
	(binf-flag)
	(if) (#receptacle is open) (then)
		(balloon rises)
	(else)
		(balloon falls)
	(endif)

%% RISE-AND-SHINE (77act2.mud:532): if the balloon is left inflated and
%% untied on a ledge, it drifts off on its own, stranding whoever got out.
%% This is what arms the volcano gnome's appearance timer (VLGIN).
(ledge room #narrow-ledge)
(ledge room #volcano-view)
(ledge room #wide-ledge)

(on every tick)
	~(#player is #in #basket2)
	(#basket2 is #in $ledge)
	(ledge room $ledge)
	(binf-flag)
	~(balloon is anchored)
	(if) (current room $ledge) (then)
		You watch as the balloon slowly floats away.  It seems to be
		ascending, due to its light load.
	(endif)
	(now) (#basket2 is nowhere)
	(now) (#volcano-gnome timer is 10)
	(now) (#volcano-gnome timer running)

%%%

%% VLBOT
#volcano-bottom
(room *)
(name *)	Volcano Bottom
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(look *)
	You are at the bottom of a large dormant volcano. High above you light
	may be seen entering from the cone of the volcano. The only exit here is
	to the north.
(from * go #north to #lava-room)

%% VAIR1
#volcano-core1
(room *)
(name *)	Volcano Core
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are about one hundred feet above the bottom of the volcano. The top
	of the volcano is clearly visible here.
%%(from * go ##!#!# to #thing)

%% VAIR2
#volcano-core2
(room *)
(name *)	Volcano Core
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are about two hundred feet above the volcano floor. Looming above is
	the rim of the volcano. There is a small ledge on the west side.
(from * go #west to #narrow-ledge)
(from * go #land to #narrow-ledge)

%% VAIR3
#volcano-core3
(room *)
(name *)	Volcano Core
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are high above the floor of the volcano. From here the rim of the
	volcano looks very narrow and you are very near it. To the east is what
	appears to be a viewing ledge, too thin to land on.
%%(from * go ##!#!# to #thing)

%% VAIR4
#volcano-core4
(room *)
(name *)	Volcano Core
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are near the rim of the volcano which is only about 15 feet across.
	To the west, there is a place to land on a wide ledge.
(from * go #land to #wide-ledge)
(from * go #east to #wide-ledge)

%% LEDG2
#narrow-ledge
(room *)
(name *)	Narrow Ledge
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(look *)
	You are on a narrow ledge overlooking the inside of an old dormant
	volcano. This ledge appears to be about in the middle between the floor
	below and the rim above. There is an exit here to the south.
(narrate failing to leave * #down)
	I wouldn't jump from here.
(from * go #east to #volcano-core2)
(from * go #launch to #volcano-core2)
(from * go #west to #volcano-bottom)
(prevent [leave * #west])
	~(gnome-door)
		You can't go that way.
(from * go #south to #library)

%% LEDG3
#volcano-view
(room *)
(name *)	Volcano View
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are on a ledge in the middle of a large volcano. Below you the
	volcano bottom can be seen and above is the rim of the volcano. A couple
	of ledges can be seen on the other side of the volcano; it appears that
	this ledge is intermediate in elevation between those on the other side.
	The exit from this room is to the east.
(narrate failing to leave * #down)
	I wouldn't try that.
(narrate failing to leave * #cross)
	It is impossible to cross this distance.
(from * go #east to #egyptian-room)

%% LEDG4
#wide-ledge
(room *)
(name *)	Wide Ledge
(inherently dark *)
(* is midair)
(look *)
	You are on a wide ledge high into the volcano.  The rim of the
   	volcano is about 200 feet above and there is a precipitous drop below
   	to the bottom.
	(if)(#dusty-room has been munged)(then)
		The way to the south is blocked by rubble.
	(else)
		There is a small door to the south.
	(endif)
%% TODO: room action routine LEDGE-FUNCTION
(narrate failing to leave * #down)
	It's a long way down!
(from * go #launch to #volcano-core4)
(from * go #west to #volcano-bottom)
(prevent [leave * #west])
	~(gnome-door)
		You can't go that way.
(from * go #south to #dusty-room)
%% MUNGED-ROOM blocks re-entry (77act2.mud SAFE-MUNG/MUNG-ROOM)
(prevent [leave * #south])
	(#dusty-room has been munged)
	The way is blocked by debris from an explosion.

%% LAVA
#lava-room
(room *)
(name *)	Lava Room
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are in a small room, whose walls are formed by an old lava flow.
	There are exits here to the west and the south.
(from * go #south to #volcano-bottom)
(from * go #west to #ruby-room)

%% GNOME
#volcano-gnome
(name *)	Volcano Gnome
(dict *)	troll gnome volcano
(animate *)
(appearance *)
	There is a nervous Volcano Gnome here.

%% VOLGNOME (77act2.mud:756): once the appearance timer (armed above, when
%% the balloon drifts off empty) runs out, the gnome walks out of the wall
%% the next time the player is standing on a ledge - polling forever, one
%% tick at a time, until that's true.
~(gnome has appeared)
~(gnome has departed)
~(gnome is nervous)

(on #volcano-gnome timeout)
	~(gnome has appeared)
	(now) (gnome ready to appear)

(late on every tick)
	(gnome ready to appear)
	~(gnome has appeared)
	(current room $room)
	(ledge room $room)
	(now) ~(gnome ready to appear)
	(now) (gnome has appeared)
	(now) (#volcano-gnome is #in $room)
	(notice #volcano-gnome)
	A volcano gnome seems to walk straight out of the wall and says
	'I have a very busy appointment schedule and little time to waste on
	tresspassers, but for a small fee, I'll show you the way out.'  You
	notice the gnome nervously glancing at his watch.

%% GNOME-FUNCTION (77act2.mud:768): give/throw a treasure, and he opens the
%% west door; give/throw anything else, and he crunches it; anything else
%% you try on him makes him more nervous, arming a one-shot 5-turn fuse
%% (GNOME-FLAG guards it from being rearmed) after which he leaves for good.
(gnome accepts $Treasure)
	(current room $room)
	(now) ($Treasure is #in $room)
	(now) (gnome-door)
	Thank you very much for (the $Treasure).  I don't believe I've ever
	seen one as beautiful.  'Follow me', he says, and a door appears on
	the west end of the ledge.  Through the door, you can see a narrow
	chimney sloping steeply downward.

(gnome crunches $Obj)
	(now) ($Obj is nowhere)
	'That wasn't quite what I had in mind', he says, crunching (the
	$Obj) in his rock-hard hands.

(instead of [give $Treasure to #volcano-gnome])
	~(gnome has departed)
	(treasure $Treasure)
	($Treasure has ancestor #player)
	(gnome accepts $Treasure)
	(tick) (stop)

(instead of [throw $Treasure at #volcano-gnome])
	~(gnome has departed)
	(treasure $Treasure)
	($Treasure has ancestor #player)
	(gnome accepts $Treasure)
	(tick) (stop)

(instead of [give $Obj to #volcano-gnome])
	~(gnome has departed)
	~(treasure $Obj)
	($Obj has ancestor #player)
	(gnome crunches $Obj)
	(tick) (stop)

(instead of [throw $Obj at #volcano-gnome])
	~(gnome has departed)
	~(treasure $Obj)
	(gnome crunches $Obj)
	(tick) (stop)

(gnome grows nervous)
	The gnome appears increasingly nervous.
	(if) ~(gnome is nervous) (then)
		(now) (gnome is nervous)
		(now) (#volcano-gnome timer is 5)
		(now) (#volcano-gnome timer running)
	(endif)

(instead of [attack #volcano-gnome with $])
	(gnome grows nervous)

(instead of [attack #volcano-gnome])
	(gnome grows nervous)

(instead of [take #volcano-gnome])
	(gnome grows nervous)

(on #volcano-gnome timeout)
	(gnome has appeared)
	~(gnome has departed)
	(now) (gnome has departed)
	(now) (#volcano-gnome is nowhere)
	The gnome glances at his watch.  'Oops.  I'm late for an
	appointment!'  He disappears, leaving you alone on the ledge.

%% BALLO
#basket2
(* is #in #volcano-bottom)
(name *)	basket
(vehicle *)
(actor container *)
(dict *)	wicker balloon
(* size is 70)
(* capacity is 100)
(appearance *)
	There is a very large and extremely heavy wicker basket with a cloth bag
	here. Inside the basket is a metal receptacle of some kind. Attached to
	the basket on the outside is a piece of wire.
	(if) (binf-flag) ($what is #in #receptacle) (then)
		The cloth bag is inflated and there is (a $what) burning in the receptacle.
	(else)
        The cloth bag is draped over the the basket.
	(endif)
	(if) (balloon is anchored) (then)
		The balloon is tied to the hook.
	(endif)

